# Local-development secrets for `wrangler dev`. Copy to `.dev.vars` (gitignored)
# and fill in. In PRODUCTION these are NOT set here — use:
#   npx wrangler secret put SUBMIT_TOKENS
#   npx wrangler secret put IP_HASH_SALT
#
# Both are REQUIRED. Without them POST /api/submit answers 503 and stores
# nothing — the endpoint fails closed rather than accepting unauthenticated
# writes or storing an unsalted (and therefore reversible) IP hash.

# Accepted app tokens, comma-separated. The iOS app sends one of these as
# `Authorization: Bearer <token>`. A LIST so a rotation has an overlap window:
# add the new token, ship the app update, then drop the old one.
SUBMIT_TOKENS="local-dev-token"

# Random 32+ character string. Salts the SHA-256 of the client IP that is stored
# as `ipHash` and used as the rate-limit key. Changing it re-anonymises every
# future submission (old hashes stop matching new ones).
IP_HASH_SALT="local-dev-salt-change-me-0123456789"
